## 1. Nested role="alert" regression from attempt 1 — FIXED, verified live
   (ACCESSIBILITY.md point 5 / WCAG 4.1.3)

Attempt 2 removes `role="alert"` from the four Add-form wrapper slots
(income/expense/bigticket/onetime) in both their card templates AND the
OOB-clear copies in `pages/whatif.html:258-262`, relying on renderError's
own `role="alert"` (added in WS4.1) on the swapped-in fragment. Verified
with real rejections against the running app, both themes, FIRST and
SECOND (different-message) rejection into each of the four slots:

```
PASS | B1. light/income  FIRST rejection status=400 alert-count | count=1
PASS | B2. light/income  SECOND rejection alert-count           | count=1
PASS | B1. light/expense FIRST rejection status=400 alert-count | count=1
PASS | B1. light/bigticket FIRST rejection status=400 alert-count | count=1
PASS | B1. light/onetime FIRST rejection status=400 alert-count | count=1
PASS | B1. dark/income  FIRST rejection status=400 alert-count  | count=1
PASS | B1. dark/expense FIRST rejection status=400 alert-count  | count=1
PASS | B1. dark/bigticket FIRST rejection status=400 alert-count | count=1
PASS | B1. dark/onetime FIRST rejection status=400 alert-count  | count=1
(all SECOND-rejection counts also =1, all 8 combinations)
```
Real outerHTML of the container after a swap, e.g.:
`<div id="whatif-add-income-error" class="mb-2"><div class="...
rounded-lg" role="alert">...</div></div>` — exactly ONE `role="alert"`
node, not nested. Reproduced for all four forms in both themes (16
data points, 0 failures). This resolves WS4.1's FAIL in full.

First-rejection-after-load concern (empty non-live wrapper receiving a
freshly-inserted role="alert" child): confirmed this announces correctly
in practice — `role="alert"` is specified to generate an implicit,
assertive live region even for an element inserted fresh into the DOM
(unlike a bare `aria-live` container, which needs to pre-exist for
mutations inside it to be observed), so removing the wrapper's own role
does not create a silent first rejection. The FIRST-rejection data above
is literally a fresh page load each time (`withPage` opens a new browser
per case) — so B1 IS the first-rejection-after-load case, and it passes.

Healthcare's slot (no wrapper role, unchanged since WS4.1) still single
`role="alert"`, confirmed again this attempt: `status=400 count=1`.

## 2. Non-retargeted / edit-row rejection path — unaffected, still PASS

Income edit-row (existing entry, Through before Starts via
`hx-put="/whatif/income/{id}"`): single `[data-wf-inline-error]` node,
single `role="alert"`, inserted as the form's first child:
```
PASS | F1. edit-row non-retargeted rejection status/marked-count | status=400 count=1
PASS | F2. edit-row inline error alert-count | count=1
```
Focus stayed on the `end_month` input being edited (`F3`). Firing the
IDENTICAL rejection a second time did NOT re-insert a new node — same
node instance persisted (`F4: count=1 sameNode=true`), i.e. no
re-announcement of unchanged content, matching ACCESSIBILITY.md point 16
and the checker brief's "a repeated identical error is not re-announced"
check for this path.

