## 8. Reflow at 320/375px — PASS for the new/changed content; one
   PRE-EXISTING, unrelated defect reconfirmed

- 375px: `document.documentElement.scrollWidth === window.innerWidth`
  (375), error fragment `scrollWidth === clientWidth` (299, no internal
  clipping).
- 320px: page `scrollWidth` = 344px (overflow) — reproduced identically
  on a **fresh page load with no error ever triggered** (baseline probe,
  344px), and the widest element is the Big-Ticket "Add Item"
  `<button class="px-3 py-1 bg-accent-strong...">`, unrelated to the
  error markup and untouched by WS4.2.diff. OBSERVATION (pre-existing,
  out of scope), matching WS4.1's identical finding.

